Oracle's security alert is the advisory published with the October 4 patch. As their titles say, Rapid7 reports the zero-day exploited in the wild, Tenable answers frequently asked questions about the CVE, and Oligo Security covers its exploitation in Cl0p extortion campaigns. MITRE's page defines T1190, Exploit Public-Facing Application, the technique behind stage 02.

The background slides name their own sources, from MITRE ATT&CK, the csoh.org glossary and OWASP.

